.TH NOTEPADX 1 "September 2026" "0.1.0" "NotepadX Manual"
.SH NAME
notepadx \- fast, distraction-free text and code editor for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notepadx
[\fB\-\-new\-window\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B NotepadX
is a fast, bloat-free Notepad++ alternative designed for Linux. It features single-instance IPC coordination via Unix domain sockets, instant multi-tab session restoration, atomic autosaving, syntax highlighting for 16+ languages via Lexilla, PCRE2 regex search and replace, bookmarks, and full keyboard shortcut ergonomics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-window\fR
Force open a new application window instead of passing file arguments to an existing running instance.
.TP
\fIFILE...\fR
One or more files to open as tabs. If NotepadX is already running, these files are immediately forwarded to the primary window.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B File Operations
.br
Ctrl+N: New tab
.br
Ctrl+O: Open file dialog
.br
Ctrl+S: Save file
.br
Ctrl+Shift+S: Save file as
.br
Ctrl+W: Close current tab
.br
Ctrl+Shift+T: Reopen last closed tab
.br
Ctrl+Q: Quit application
.TP
.B Navigation & Tabs
.br
Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab: Next / Previous tab
.br
Alt+1 .. Alt+9: Switch directly to tab 1 through 9
.TP
.B Search & Bookmarks
.br
Ctrl+F: Find
.br
Ctrl+H: Replace
.br
F3 / Shift+F3: Find next / previous
.br
Ctrl+G: Go to line dialog
.br
Ctrl+F2: Toggle bookmark on current line
.br
F2 / Shift+F2: Jump to next / previous bookmark
.br
Ctrl+Shift+F2: Clear all bookmarks
.TP
.B Editing & Line Ops
.br
Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y: Undo / Redo
.br
Ctrl+D: Duplicate line
.br
Ctrl+L: Delete line
.br
Alt+Up / Alt+Down: Move line up / down
.br
Alt+Z: Toggle word wrap
.br
Ctrl++ / Ctrl+\- / Ctrl+0: Zoom in / Zoom out / Reset zoom
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/NotepadX/settings.json
User preferences (font, font size, tab width, line numbers, word wrap, dark/light theme, recent files).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/NotepadX/session.json
Saved session state containing open tabs, file paths, cursor positions, and scroll offsets.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/NotepadX/unnamed_tabs/
Atomic backing store for untitled, unsaved tabs.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/notepadx.sock
Unix domain socket used for single-instance IPC communication.
.SH AUTHORS
NotepadX Authors (GPLv3).
